  m_Name: Debrief_Final
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: LastSignal.Core::LastSignal.DebriefCard
  title: "Call Home"
  concept: "Deep-space communications and light-time delay"
  nasaSource: "NASA Deep Space Network (JPL, Space Communications and Navigation program)"
  body: "The Deep Space Network's large dishes at Goldstone, Madrid and Canberra keep in touch with every deep-space mission, and between them one site can always see a spacecraft. Radio travels at the speed of light: a message from Mars takes about 3 to 22 minutes, and one from Voyager 1 takes about a day. A spacecraft's high-gain antenna must point precisely at Earth to be heard."
